{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>From the labor.</b> That is, they did not cry out to El to save them, but rather they cried out from pain, like a person who cries out from his suffering. And Scripture informs us that that cry ascended before HaShem — and that is what is meant by <b>their cry</b> etc. <b>from the labor</b>: meaning, from the pain of the labor. <b>And HaShem heard their groaning</b> (Exodus 2:24): meaning, the raising of the sound of their pain." "<b>Further,</b> it intends along the lines of the verse (Psalms 118:5): ״מִן הַמֵּצַר קָרָאתִי יָּהּ עָנָנִי בַמֶּרְחָב יָהּ״ — for one of the prayers that are accepted is a prayer that comes from within distress, and so it says (Jonah 2:3): ״קָרָאתִי מִצָּרָה״. And that is what is meant by <b>and their cry ascended</b> etc. <b>from the labor</b>: meaning, because it was from the distress of the labor. And accordingly, this cry is both a prayer and a cry of the pain of distress — and behold, it is alluded to in His saying ״from the labor and they cried out.״ And on this basis the precise reason is correctly established for why Scripture changed its language, beginning with ״וַיִּזְעָקוּ וַתַּעַל שַׁוְעָתָם״ etc., when it should have said ״וַתַּעַל זַעֲקָתָם״ etc. Rather, Scripture intended to say that they cried out from the distress and also cried out to HaShem, as stated: ״וַתַּעַל שַׁוְעָתָם״. And accordingly the versification of Scripture is as follows: ״וַתַּעַל שַׁוְעָתָם״ — that they cried out to Elohim, from the labor." "Or it may further be that His saying <b>from the labor</b> intends that the cry did not reach before HaShem by way of an intermediary, but rather it ascended directly — from the labor to Elohim — not by way of ״a bird of the wings [i.e., an intermediary] telling the matter״ (Ecclesiastes 10:20)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:45.442621725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}